  "notes": "USAGE:\nOften used with する as {多読|たどく}する. Frequently contrasted with {精読|せいどく} (intensive, careful reading). In language education, {多読|たどく} has become a well-known methodology where learners read large amounts of easy material to build fluency naturally.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {多読|たどく}する (to read extensively)\n- {多読|たどく}{法|ほう} (extensive reading method)\n- {英語|えいご}{多読|たどく} (extensive reading in English)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {精読|せいどく}: intensive reading — reading carefully for full comprehension (opposite approach)\n- {乱読|らんどく}: reading indiscriminately, without a plan or system",
